    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.trailspace\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently there are functions to show or hide trailing whitespace with `mini.trailspace`, but from what I can see no way to toggle showing/hiding whitespace. It would be nice to have such a function that can be bound to a keymap.",
